   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote it as one macrocyclic SMILES. I checked each stereocentre against the drawn wedges and hashes by hand and did not run it through a parser.\n\n**Macrocycle, in order around the ring:**\n- **Eight-membered lactam:** the ring contains a cis C=C and a C=O, and its alpha carbon carries an N-methyl amide nitrogen.\n- **Cyclohexylmethyl residue:** the lactam nitrogen is attached to a CH bearing a CH2 and a 4,4-difluorocyclohexyl group, followed by C(=O)\u2013N(Me)\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH.\n- **Aryl residue:** the next CH carries a CH2CH2 chain to a 3-chloro-4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl ring, then C(=O).\n- **Pyrrolidine:** 4-methylpyrrolidine-2-carbonyl, followed by NH on a 3,3-dimethylcyclobutane carbon.\n- **N-methyl isoleucine-type residue:** C(=O)\u2013N(Me)\u2013CH(sec-butyl)\u2013C(=O).\n- **Aspartic-type residue:** N(Me)\u2013CH(C(=O)NMe2)\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O).\n- **O-propyl serine:** N(Me)\u2013CH(CH2OCH2CH2CH3)\u2013C(=O).\n- **Isoleucine:** NH\u2013CH(CH(CH3)CH2CH3)\u2013C(=O).\n- **Closure:** C(=O)\u2013N(Me)\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O) returns to the N-methyl nitrogen on the lactam alpha carbon.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each centre from the wedges and hashes and then converted to @/@@ by neighbour order.\n- Lactam alpha carbon: S.\n- The CH bearing the difluorocyclohexylmethyl group: R.\n- The arylethyl CH: S.\n- Pyrrolidine C2 and C4: both S.\n- N-methyl isoleucine-type alpha carbon: S.\n- Aspartic-type alpha carbon: S.\n- Serine alpha carbon: S.\n- Isoleucine alpha and beta carbons: both S.\n- The sec-butyl CH, the cyclobutane carbons and the ring double bond (cis) follow the drawing; the sec-butyl CH has no wedge and gets no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: CN9[C@H]1C/C=C\\CCN(C1=O)[C@H](CC2CCC(F)(F)CC2)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCc3ccc(C(F)(F)F)c(Cl)c3)C(=O)N4C[C@@H](C)C[C@H]4C(=O)NC5(CC(C)(C)C5)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)CC)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](COCCC)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)N(C)CC9=O)C(=O)N(C)C"
